[{"answer":"Canada is one of the largest countries in the world.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/1.mp3"},{"answer":"It is located in the northern half of the continent of North America, above the United States.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/2.mp3"},{"answer":"Canada is divided into ten provinces and three territories,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/3.mp3"},{"answer":"each of which is different from the others.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/4.mp3"},{"answer":"The province of British Columbia is located at the far western end of Canada.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/5.mp3"},{"answer":"British Columbia stretches from the Pacific Ocean, at the west,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/6.mp3"},{"answer":"to the Rocky Mountains, at the east.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/7.mp3"},{"answer":"British Columbia contains the city of Vancouver, where two million people live.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Most of the land of British Columbia is very mountainous,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/9.mp3"},{"answer":"with vast forests covering the mountains.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/10.mp3"},{"answer":"In British Columbia, forestry is an important industry,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/11.mp3"},{"answer":"providing wood for people around the world.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/12.mp3"},{"answer":"Moving east from British Columbia, the next provinces are","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/13.mp3"},{"answer":"Alberta, Saskatchewan, and Manitoba.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/14.mp3"},{"answer":"These are known as the prairie provinces,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/15.mp3"},{"answer":"because they are mostly made of flat, grassy land called \"prairie\".","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/16.mp3"},{"answer":"Alberta is the province where the flat prairie meets the tall beautiful Rocky Mountains.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/17.mp3"},{"answer":"In Alberta, there are many fields where oil and gas are found,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/18.mp3"},{"answer":"and there are also many farms where cattle are raised.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/19.mp3"},{"answer":"Saskatchewan is the province that grows the most wheat.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/20.mp3"},{"answer":"Wheat from Saskatchewan is sent around the world","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/21.mp3"},{"answer":"to make bread and pasta for many people.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/22.mp3"},{"answer":"Manitoba is the other prairie province.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/23.mp3"},{"answer":"Its largest city, Winnipeg, is about halfway between the Pacific and Atlantic oceans.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/24.mp3"},{"answer":"Winnipeg has the coldest winters of any large city in the world,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/25.mp3"},{"answer":"with temperatures sometimes reaching -40 degrees Celsius!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Moving east, the next province is Ontario.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/27.mp3"},{"answer":"The land in the northern part of Ontario is very rocky","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/28.mp3"},{"answer":"and contains many thousands and thousands of lakes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/29.mp3"},{"answer":"Many mines are found in northern Ontario.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/30.mp3"},{"answer":"In the southern part of Ontario, there is good farmland,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/31.mp3"},{"answer":"and there are also many cities where factories produce cars and steel.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/32.mp3"},{"answer":"Ontario contains Canada's largest city, Toronto,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/33.mp3"},{"answer":"as well as the capital city of Canada - Ottawa.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/34.mp3"},{"answer":"In the southern part of Ontario are four of the largest lakes in the world,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/35.mp3"},{"answer":"known as the Great Lakes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/36.mp3"},{"answer":"Next to Ontario is the province of Quebec.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/37.mp3"},{"answer":"Unlike the other provinces, where most people speak English,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/38.mp3"},{"answer":"most of the people in Quebec speak French.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/39.mp3"},{"answer":"The capital of Quebec is called Quebec City,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/40.mp3"},{"answer":"and this is one of the oldest cities in North America.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/41.mp3"},{"answer":"Quebec City contains many buildings that are hundreds of years old.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/42.mp3"},{"answer":"Also in the province of Quebec is the city of Montreal.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/43.mp3"},{"answer":"Of all the French-speaking cities in the world, only Paris is larger than Montreal!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/44.mp3"},{"answer":"In the eastern part of Canada are the Atlantic provinces,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/45.mp3"},{"answer":"which are next to the Atlantic Ocean.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/46.mp3"},{"answer":"These provinces are New Brunswick, Nova Scotia,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/47.mp3"},{"answer":"Prince Edward Island, and Newfoundland.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/48.mp3"},{"answer":"In the Atlantic provinces, fishing is an important industry.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/49.mp3"},{"answer":"Tourism is also important as many people come to see the beauty of these provinces.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/50.mp3"},{"answer":"The people in these provinces are said to be the friendliest in Canada.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/51.mp3"},{"answer":"In the far north of Canada are the three territories that lie beside the Arctic Ocean:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/52.mp3"},{"answer":"Yukon, Northwest Territories, and Nunavut.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/53.mp3"},{"answer":"Many of the people in these territories are the Native people of Canada,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/54.mp3"},{"answer":"known as the Indians and the Inuit.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/55.mp3"},{"answer":"The northern areas have very cold, dark winters.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/56.mp3"},{"answer":"The summer is short, but the days are very long and bright.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/167-canada-provinces-and-territories-2019-04-07-04-36-49/57.mp3"}]
